Response and Request bodies made from a string or bytes are byte streams, as
the Fetch standard has them, so BYOB readers work on them; each read gets a
copy, since enqueueing on a byte stream transfers (detaches) the chunk's
buffer. (fetch/api/response/response-consume-stream.any.js; Deno has the
same gap.)

